      ],
      "impact": "With a 10 M\u03a9 pull-up instead of 10 k\u03a9, the OLED RES# line is held high extremely weakly. Input leakage and noise on the long DISP_RES trace (and the MCU pin's high-Z state at power-up) can pull RES# low or cause it to float, leading to spurious resets, a display that fails to initialise, or intermittent blanking \u2014 behaviour different from the intended 10 k\u03a9 design.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic matches the specification everywhere except the DISP_RES pull-up: R4 is drawn as 10 M\u03a9 rather than the specified 10 k\u03a9, a three-decade error that weakly holds the SSD1306 reset line and can cause spurious resets / display-initialisation failures."
}

